&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Xometry (NASDAQ: XMTR) powers the industries of today and tomorrow by connecting the people with big ideas to the manufacturers who can bring them to life. Xometry’s digital marketplace gives manufacturers the critical resources they need to grow their business while also making it easy for buyers at Fortune 1000 companies to tap into global manufacturing capacity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly organized and client-savvy Website Project Manager to serve as the engine behind our website build delivery for mid-market manufacturing clients. This is a unique opportunity for a solution-oriented project management practitioner to bridge the gap between technical B2B buyers and the internal teams who bring their websites to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will thrive at the intersection of client relationship management and operational delivery, specializing in translating ambiguous, non-marketing language from manufacturing clients into clear, actionable direction for designers, developers, and content editors. As both the client&#39;s primary point of contact and the internal team&#39;s source of truth, you will own the end-to-end lifecycle of standard and mid-complexity website build projects, from kickoff through launch, ensuring they are delivered on schedule, within scope, and within budget — without requiring daily oversight from leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You&#39;ll Contribute:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Delivery &amp;amp; Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own project delivery end-to-end, leading post-sale website build projects from kickoff to launch with minimal daily oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage resourcing to keep project velocity on pace with milestones by coordinating with department heads to secure design and development resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate quality assurance and risk mitigation by working with QA to confirm deliverables meet internal and client standards, and identify and resolve risks before they affect the timeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Relationship Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary client contact for assigned manufacturing clients: run client meetings, deliver weekly status updates, and turn client input into clear direction for internal teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decode client intent for the internal team by employing analytical skills and curiosity to determine their true business needs, especially when their feedback does not align cleanly with standard marketing terms (e.g., inquiring about their standard customer profile rather than asking for a “target persona”)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide projects toward sound solutions by gathering usable feedback on deliverables, offering real-time resolutions, and clearly relaying client feedback to production team members for implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scope, Budget &amp;amp; Documentation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protect project scope and margin by proactively flagging scope creep early, discussing scope expansion or preservation solutions with clients, and communicating contract adjustments with sales partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author and maintain project documentation that serves as the team&#39;s source of truth: project schedules, creative briefs, and functional requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic UX &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and address user experience deficiencies by providing clients with strategic counsel on content organization, structural navigation adjustments, call-to-action optimizations, and module layout implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross-project with Senior PMs and Digital Marketing Managers on enterprise accounts that run concurrently with a client&#39;s website project&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring to TMS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Project management experience with demonstrated success managing multiple simultaneous projects at varying levels of complexity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Solution-Oriented Mindset: &lt;/strong&gt;Strong critical thinking and adaptability under changing project conditions, with the ability to decode ambiguous or unconventional client requests, translate them for internal teams, and propose alternatives that keep a project within scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Fluency: &lt;/strong&gt;Practical understanding of how websites function, including the ability to make minor edits (text changes, image swaps) directly in WordPress or HubSpot. Proficiency with Asana or comparable project management software, and Google Workspace (Docs, Sheets, Slides, Drive, Gmail, Calendar). Comfort working across Zoom, Microsoft Teams, and Slack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Stakeholder Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Working understanding of B2B user experience principles in digital environments, and comfort asking clarifying, non-jargon questions of clients who may not have marketing vocabulary or clearly defined audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Hybrid, based in Lexington, KY; Waltham, MA; or North Bethesda, MD (or GSS, pending HR determination)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a digital or marketing agency, specifically in a client-facing delivery role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CAPM or PMP certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on WordPress administration experience beyond basic content edits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior exposure to manufacturing, industrial, or other technical B2B clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI tools such as Gemini or Claude to speed up documentation and communication work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Xometry is an equal opportunity employer. All applicants will be considered for employment without attention to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran, or disability status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;For US based roles: Xometry participates in E-Verify and after a job offer is accepted, will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the U.S.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Xometry (NASDAQ: XMTR) powers the industries of today and tomorrow by connecting the people with big ideas to the manufacturers who can bring them to life. Xometry’s digital marketplace gives manufacturers the critical resources they need to grow their business while also making it easy for buyers at Fortune 1000 companies to tap into global manufacturing capacity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;This role will provide a broad range of legal support focusing on legal operations, corporate governance, and global subsidiary management, as well as assist in establishing, maintaining, and updating the Xometry legal and regulatory compliance programs. You will work with cross-functional business units to assess their needs in alignment with Xometry&#39;s compliance requirements, in some cases owning the programs, drafting policies, educational training, and enforcement protocols to be used by the organization supporting a culture of compliance. Finally, this role will lead the legal operations function of our department.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
